%% Negative SRSW fixture.  glp.tex Remark "Guards and SRSW" (GLP-Spec
%% 831f315): "if the success of a guard implies that X? is bound to a ground
%% term, then both X and X? may occur multiple times in the clause."  Without
%% such a guard a writer occurs once (Definitions "Single-Occurrence (SO)
%% Invariant" and "GLP Program"): X in the head and again in the body under
%% known/1, which does not imply groundness, and R twice in the head with no
%% guard, are each refused.  The positive counterpart, the same writers under
%% integer/1 and ground/1, is srsw/ground_writer_multi_ok.glp.
procedure w(_?, _).
w(X, Y?) :- known(X?) | Y = s(X).

procedure two(_?, _?).
two(R, R) :- true.
